## GRADING (binding; capability decides, a comparison only finds candidates)
- **G-1 delta and claims.** **Blocker:** a path beyond the one; a byte under `src`, `docs`, `web`, `.github`, `scripts`, `infra`, `tools`; a removed or edited line among the first 585 lines of the test file or a test name lost; the head moved; a person's name, real price, BID, SKU, customer name or secret in an added line or the commit message. **Major:** a builder claim your measurement contradicts where it matters (1 commit, 1 path, +89 -0, rows 3 / names 6, the 14 survivors red, the product blob unchanged, 435/183/3048 at the unmerged head); names added other than 6; a proof that rests on a file other than the committed one (C4 f). A claim inconsistency that changes no fact (a transcription, the 3050 listed versus 3048 executed): **Note**.
- **G-2 kill proof (each is a NO GO 2 of 2).** **Major of the class:** any of the 14 round-1 survivors still green under the 38 rows (or any of the three findings' fix-shapes unmet); a variant of the C2 battery that survives every committed row and that a test-only row kills; a row that cannot fail; a row whose expectation is read from the code under test; any round-1 kill now green. **Minor, one ticket-shaped line each:** a survivor that no test-only row can kill and that is equivalent by program (a FACT); a survivor that ALSO survives at `-mut-base` (pre-existing); an assertion pinned by no mutant. **Note:** the builder's equivalents when you prove them; a build-red variant that needed a discard read. A controls failure (c0/c1/c2 red, c3 red, cw-weak not behaving) = the instrument is broken: re-do, never a finding.
- **G-3 stability, Linux.** A row that fails or flakes in your runs = Major; a construct that fails on `ubuntu-latest` (cited behaviour) = Major; unprovable = UNMEASURED. **G-5 CI line.** A warning, a failed or skipped test, a non-zero rc at the combined tree = Blocker; a count contradicting a prediction where it should agree = Major; a red you reproduce 3 of 3 alone = Blocker; a flaky red you cannot reproduce = Note. **G-6 CI and CodeQL.** The branch has no PR: **CodeQL NOT SCANNED** is the state, never clean; a verdict that needs CodeQL is conditional. If a PR exists at the verdict: a failing check-run = Major; an analysis missing = Major; a NEW alert high or higher or rule severity `error` = Blocker; a check `in_progress`: `CI pending: <names>`, conditional. **G-7 overlap, merge.** A path shared with a live lane or open PR = Major; a conflict marker against current main or an open PR head = Major for the order; the squash tree not equal to the combined tree = Major. **G-8 hygiene.** A ticket key, finding id or mutant id in a NEW code line, comment, test name or commit message = Major; non-ASCII in added lines = Major; a gitleaks hit = Blocker. **G-9 docs.** A sentence made false = Major (to the product owner's card); an absent sentence = Note.
- **Verdict token.** **GO** needs: the three fix-shapes met and the 14 survivors red under the gate's own mutants, no variant of the C2 battery surviving that a test row kills, the CI line green at the combined tree, CodeQL scanned at the PR with both thresholds met (impossible before a PR: so with no PR the best token is GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS `conditional`). **GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS** = Minor or Note only. **NO GO** = any Blocker or Major (list each by id with its class). A required check you could not run makes the first and last lines add ` (conditional: <reason>)`; a C2 or C3 that could not be run is always conditional. **At this round a NO GO is NO GO 2 of 2 on the class: THE CAP. No third round is opened by you or by a builder.** **Prediction (the drafter's, to be beaten or confirmed, never copied): GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS (conditional: CodeQL NOT SCANNED), because the builder rebuilt the gate's 14 from its text and killed all 14, the live risks being (i) a variant of the same family the gate did not name (a seed on the section id counter, a half seed, the required entry suppressed when the budget is spent, a count error hidden once 20 nulls are listed) that the three rows' typed lists do not separate, (ii) the interruption: a mutant pass measured on a test-file state that is not the committed blob, (iii) the 38 rows' weight on the 20-minute job (the new rows are 25-element bodies, so a small risk).**

## VERDICT
First line of STATUS: `GATE VERDICT B763: branch b745/mps-walk-caps <GO|GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS|NO GO> round 2 of 2 (the cap; NO GO here is NO GO 2 of 2 on the class, no third round, a card for the product owner; NO GO 1 of 2 before this gate, no PR yet) @ db57178 on main <sha7> (C1 delta <1 commit, 1 path, +89 -0 y/n> removed test lines 0 <y/n> first 585 lines byte-equal <y/n> product blob unchanged <y/n> names lost <n> added <6 y/n> hygiene hits <n> - C2 fix-shapes met <k of 3> rows green at head <y/n> predictions equal <y/n> - C3 round-1 survivors killed <k of 14> own variants <n> killed <k> equivalent <q proved y/n> build-red re-run <r> survivors <names|none> seeded <k of 4> kills retained <k of 20> pre-existing <names|none> - C4 controls c0 c1 c2 c3 cw-weak <as expected y/n> rows with no killer <n> audit of the interruption <match y/n> - C5 build warnings <n> Engine/Import/Api <e/i/a> failed <n> skipped <n> 3 runs <green y/n> zone and culture <y/n> - C6 docs <not needed y/n> CodeQL <NOT SCANNED|counts> checks <what they read> conflicts <n> overlap <n> main moved <y/n> - C7 gitleaks canary rc <n> scan rc <n> Jira <MET/PARTLY/NOT MET each|NOT READ> residue <none|named>) majors+: <ids, or none>`. A NO GO line ends with `majors+: B763-n, ...` naming every Major and Blocker by id and its class (for the card). Then the sections as the template's VERDICT list (Step 0 / REFUSE counts / PINS at start, mid, verdict / instrument and load / predictions with evidence paths / C1-C7 / the battery tables (yours, with the builder's beside it) / the row -> credited killers table / the Pass A and Pass B tables / merge table / findings `B763-n` with severity, `path:line`, instrument, FAIL met, GRADING id, fix-shape in prose, the regression that would be red, evidence class / FOR TUESDAY / **ROUND-CAP STATEMENT** (both counts above; the CLOSED instances and the RESIDUE, each named with its evidence, so the product owner's card can say what ships and what is ticketed; a NO GO here does not open round 3: say what each open finding would need and in which commit it sits (commit 1 = the supplies walk, commit 2 = the BOM walks, commit 3 = the rows)) / FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections / processes, slots, trees left / **UNMEASURED** last). **Last line, exactly one of:** `VERDICT: B763 b745/mps-walk-caps @ <sha7> <GO|GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS|NO GO> (round 2 of 2, the cap; CodeQL <NOT SCANNED|counts>; CI <local green|pending: names>) on main <sha7>` (`<sha7>` after `@` = the head you gated; after `main` by `ls-remote` at the verdict; findings with severities on the line above; no landing words) or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` + ONE question.

## LANDING, MERGE AND HOLD (Tuesday's; you write it into FOR TUESDAY and do none of it)
MPS lands by SQUASH with the head pinned (`1_Project_Definition/CLARIFICATIONS.md:809` and `:854`, quoted above; project `CLAUDE.md:50-52`: the org ruleset requires CodeQL results on `main`; seats push a branch only). Tuesday opens the PR from `b745/mps-walk-caps` AFTER your verdict, reads the 4 CodeQL analyses and the `dotnet` check on the PR's merge ref (the branch is based on `2e7f9d8a`; main is `1137f119`, so GitHub merges them and checks THAT tree), and then runs `gh pr merge <n> -R datasecau/MPS-Commercial-Calculator --squash --match-head-commit db57178676ee253479677fbcd723419fbc90ea9c`; you never merge, push, comment, mark ready, open a PR or re-run a check. With three commits the squash subject is the PR title (Tuesday's text) and the body lists the three commit messages: write into FOR TUESDAY what the squash will carry (three attribution lines). **NOT deployed:** a merge is not a deploy, MPS hosted is one card per deploy. A GO or GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS: the records seat, not this seat, moves MPSCALC-338 and MPSCALC-339 and ticket-shapes the residue. A NO GO (the cap): per the cap rule the closed instances ship and the residue is ticketed, and WHICH is a card for the product owner; you only say which instances are closed and which are residue, never whether to ship.

## LOAD (binding; the MPS heavy-slot convention)
8 cores. Heavy = `dotnet restore`, `build`, `test` (including `--list-tests` and every mutant build and run), the full CI line, every scratch-merge build. Git, `gh` GETs and Jira GETs are light. **Start a heavy run only while `LC_ALL=C uptime` load1 is below 7** at two reads 4 s apart (not independent: say so), recorded beside the result; at 7 or over poll every 20 s and log; do light work meanwhile (C1, predictions, the table written from source, C6, the clone, Jira). **Then take ONE slot atomically:** `mkdir '<project>/.tools/heavy-slot-1' 2>/dev/null || mkdir '<project>/.tools/heavy-slot-2' 2>/dev/null || mkdir '<project>/.tools/heavy-slot-3'`, write `B763 <start> <label>` into its `holder`; read every other holder first (drafter at 21:5x: `heavy-slot-1` `B752 21:27:00 web`, `heavy-slot-2` `B757 21:54:22 m341`, `heavy-slot-3` ABSENT; a holder that looks stale is reported, never removed; a slot directory with no holder file is reported, never taken over; **the gate waits for a free slot and never takes a held one**). All taken: wait 3 minutes and retry. One slot, one heavy job at a time; re-read load1 at the start of EACH job inside a held slot; for a run longer than a few minutes hold `.tools/b763/heavy.lock` (a directory, pid inside, released by a MOVE). Release ONLY your own slot by a MOVE into `.tools/_quarantine/2026-10-26_B763_<slot>_<label>/`, never `rm`. The shared `.tools/.git-lock` wraps GIT REF WRITES ONLY. **A MOVING heartbeat** (counter plus `date`) goes to `.tools/b763/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job. A wait loop never uses `pgrep -f` or `ps | grep` on a pattern in its own command line (wait on a pid with `kill -0`, `wait $!`, or a done-marker file). Release the slot between the whole-solution run and the mutant matrix so the other seats can take one. NO artificial load. **NuGet homes SEAT-LOCAL**, proven. Budget guide: about 50 to 70 narrow mutant builds and class runs (each one build plus a 38-row class run, DevStub only for the matrix, both providers for c0 and the final run), one whole-solution run (the CI line; the builder's took 444 s for the test step, against the 20-minute cap), two differential batches, one cw-weak pair.

