- Datasec / MPS Commercial Calculator only. No deploy, `az`, Kudu, Entra, Graph, docker, ssh. **No HTTP to any hosted or production site or app host** (the Api tests host in process). Network: the one explicit-refspec `git fetch` of Step 1 into YOUR clone, `gh api -X GET` under the project `GH_CONFIG_DIR`, Jira GET as C7 allows, the NuGet restore into your seat-local cache. `gh run rerun`, `gh workflow run`, `gh api -X POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE` forbidden. Never dismiss an alert. No decision-queue tool in any form, no scoreboard, no Artifact, Docs, mail, chat or publish tool. No web, node, npm or Playwright.
- **Git in the project repo `2_Project_Files`: READ verbs only** (`--no-optional-locks`: `ls-remote`, `log`, `show`, `diff`, `cat-file`, `ls-tree`, `rev-parse`, `rev-list`, `merge-base`, `grep`, `config --get`, `remote get-url`); `clone --no-hardlinks` FROM it; `fetch`, `worktree add`, `checkout --detach`, legacy `merge-tree`, `merge-tree --write-tree`, scratch `merge`/`branch` only inside `.tools/b763/repo` and `.tools/wt-b763-*`. No git verb in the project root. **Forbidden everywhere:** `merge-tree --write-tree` in the shared repo, `gc`, `worktree prune`, `reset` in the shared repo, `clean`, `stash`, `fetch --prune`, `--shared`, `--reference`.
- **Not yours (never read to obey, edit, quarantine, kill, stop or lock-break):** `b754`, `wt-b754-*` (the finished round-2 builder M34: its trees, scripts, scratch, mutant tables, probes and `out/` files are READ-FORBIDDEN for the mutant method; the published STATUS is readable; rebuild your battery from the TEXT of the round-1 findings and the source; the builder's scripts and outputs are never opened), `b745`, `wt-b745-*` (the round-1 builder, same rule), `b748`, `wt-b748-*` (the round-1 gate's trees: read-forbidden; its PUBLISHED STATUS and evidence text files under `Briefs/2026-10-26_B748_evidence/` may be read as claims, its mutant scripts only AFTER your own battery table is written), `b757`, `wt-b757-*` (MPS-M35, LIVE, holds heavy-slot-2), `b752`, `wt-b752-*` (MPS-G153, LIVE, holds heavy-slot-1), `b744`, `wt-b744-*`, `b758`, `wt-b758-*`, `b740`, `wt-b740-*`, `b732`, `b731`, `b722`, `b720`, `b717`, `b715`, `b711`, `b700*`, `b692`, `b686`, `b678*`, `b663*`, `b654`, `b645`, `b5*`, `qa-*`, `backup-*`, `_quarantine*`, every other seat's `.tools/b6*` and `.tools/b7*`. Name everything of yours `b763` / `G156`. The shared SDK `.tools/dotnet/` is read-only.
- **Real price books are confidential.** Never open `2_Project_Files/.local/`, `1_Project_Definition/Source_Documents/`, `.tools/backup-*`, or any real book or store; every scratch row is synthetic (the test file's own invented ids and `SyntheticSources`). Secrets only as environment. Never open `4_Credentials/.env` except by NAME for the Jira GET.
- **Never delete** (`rm`, `git branch -D`): quarantine to `.tools/b763/quarantine/`. **Never `cd`**; absolute single-quoted paths (they contain a space and `!`); `bash -c '...'` or a QUOTED heredoc where a path with spaces is in command position; quote URLs holding `?`; no unquoted word starting with `=` (use `----`); bash, not zsh, for loops; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count (`-E`, no `-P`); `python3 -I` for anything reading a file you did not write; write `${VAR}:path`, never `$VAR:path` (zsh reads `$h:t` as a modifier). Never kill a process by basename. No person's name in any id, file, branch or STATUS (say "the product owner"), no decision-card id.
